0..50 Comment "// A definition\'s own value that runs a pure call."
51..53 Comment "//"
54..124 Comment "// A definition\'s own value has no computation around it to run a call"
125..202 Comment "// before. A pure call there stands as the value it returns. Each read of the"
203..277 Comment "// definition runs the call, and a type that reads the definition converts"
278..353 Comment "// through the call. An effectful call there is refused `UnenclosedRun`, in"
354..398 Comment "// `ledger/diagnostics/UnenclosedRun.gandr`."
399..401 Comment "//"
402..449 Comment "// - see: #4812 — `odd`, `flipped`, `sameOdd`"
450..520 Comment "// - see: `basics/literal-in-value.gandr` — a literal a reader reads"
